    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "13. INSPECT VALVE SPRINGS"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "(a) Using a steel square, check the squareness of the valve springs."
    },
    {
      "type": "diagram",
      "index": 2,
      "description": "Valve spring squareness check using steel square",
      "labels": [
        "Squareness"
      ],
      "bbox": {
        "top": 18,
        "left": 4,
        "width": 38,
        "height": 16
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Maximum: 2.0 mm (0.079 in.)"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "If squareness is greater than maximum, replace the valve spring."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "(b) Measure the free height of all springs."
    },
    {
      "type": "diagram",
      "index": 3,
      "description": "Measuring valve spring free height with measuring tool",
      "labels": [
        "E30801"
      ],
      "bbox": {
        "top": 36,
        "left": 4,
        "width": 38,
        "height": 16
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Free height:"
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "headers": [],
      "rows": [
        [
          "Intake side",
          "49.1 mm (1.933 in.)"
        ],
        [
          "Exhaust side",
          "52.5 mm (2.067 in.)"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Replace any spring that is not correct."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "(c) Using a spring tester, check the tension of each spring at the specified installed height."
    },
    {
      "type": "diagram",
      "index": 4,
      "description": "Spring tester device with gauge and spring compression mechanism",
      "labels": [
        "E30031"
      ],
      "bbox": {
        "top": 54,
        "left": 4,
        "width": 38,
        "height": 16
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Installed height:"
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "headers": [],
      "rows": [
        [
          "Intake side",
          "40.0 mm (1.575 in.)"
        ],
        [
          "Exhaust side",
          "43.0 mm (1.693 in.)"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Installed tension:"
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "headers": [],
      "rows": [
        [
          "Intake side",
          "34.7 — 38.3 kg"
        ],
        [
          "",
          "(76.5 — 84.4 lb, 340 — 376 N)"
        ],
        [
          "Exhaust side",
          "33.3 — 36.7 kg"
        ],
        [
          "",
          "(73.4 — 80.9 lb, 327 — 360 N)"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "If not within the installed tension specification, replace the spring."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "14. INSPECT INTAKE, EXHAUST MANIFOLDS AND AIR IN-TAKE CHAMBER"
    },
    {
      "type": "diagram",
      "index": 5,
      "description": "Checking manifold surface flatness with straight edge and feeler gauge",
      "labels": [
        "LW165"
      ],
      "bbox": {
        "top": 72,
        "left": 4,
        "width": 38,
        "height": 16
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Using a precision straight edge and feeler gauge, check the surfaces contacting the cylinder head for warpage."
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "headers": [],
      "rows": [
        [
          "Maximum intake warpage:",
          "0.1 mm (0.004 in.)"
        ],
        [
